- Script creation now allocates Object.create(Script.prototype) if
  original Script class is registered; otherwise early startup scripts use
  Object.prototype. Original prefix-installed Script.prototype methods are
  inherited, not copied onto every script. Tests verify instance identity,
  method receiver and inherited/native properties.
- Script drop removes the lookup property entirely using 'delete' rather
  than overwriting with undefined. Previously retained script JSValues
  remain valid, and re-registering the same script name creates a fresh
  independent script identity. Injection-like names are rejected.
- Original script event call variant now returns arbitrary owned JSValue
  objects, not only a called flag. Values remain owned by JSTask until
  JS_Free. Native guest saw object result {sum:44,valid:1}, missing
  event=success with called=0, deliberate exception=1 and called=0,
  recovery call=success with same correct object result. All seven DONE
  notifications arrived; four ObjC game task RPCs. Clean shutdown.
- Existing OOGFOSScriptObjectEvent discards the returned owned value
  explicitly and remains backward source-compatible with prior caller.

These are actual AC090 guest tests with selector-compatible Objective-C
fixtures, not full original Oolite gameplay/ship universe.
